    "blurb": "The Omni show delivers a blistering first half highlighted by a debut Peggy‑O and tight China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider. The second set builds into an electrifying Eyes Of The World → Morning Dew climax, with strong contributions from Keith on Rhodes and Looks Like Rain. Soundboard recordings capture the performance in crystal‑clear detail.",
    "review": "December 12, 1973 at Atlanta’s Omni finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. Jerry rides a flawless tone through a debut Peggy‑O, then lets his lead soar on the iconic Eyes Of The World → Morning Dew stretch, while Phil drops massive bass bombs that lift the whole band. Keith’s Rhodes adds a shimmering layer to Looks Like Rain and his Moog textures enrich Row Jimmy, giving the set a lush harmonic backdrop. Billy’s drums are fast‑paced and lock tightly with Phil’s low end, driving the high‑octane flow from Mississippi Half-Step Uptown Toodeloo through the closing Weather Report Suite. The soundboard sources—especially the remastered gd1973-12-12.sbd.remaster.102910.flac16—present a crisp, well‑balanced mix that lets every instrument shine, making this one of ’73’s most compelling recordings.",
